  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAre the deadlines for filing corporate income tax returns the same as those for individual income tax returns in the Philippines?\n\n### Short Answer\nNo, the deadlines for filing corporate income tax returns differ from those for individual income tax returns. Corporate income tax returns are generally due on the 15th day of the fourth month following the close of the taxable year, while individual income tax returns are due on April 15 of the following year.\n\n### Accounting Treatment\nFor corporate entities, the accounting period typically aligns with the fiscal year or calendar year, depending on the corporation's choice. The corporate income tax return must reflect the income and expenses for the entire accounting period, and the return must be filed within the prescribed deadline to avoid penalties.\n\n### Tax Treatment\nUnder Section 27 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), corporations are subject to a 25% income tax rate on their taxable income derived from all sources within and without the Philippines. For individuals, Section 24 of the NIRC imposes graduated tax rates based on taxable income, with specific deadlines for filing returns.\n\n### Differences and Reconciliation\nThe key differences in deadlines stem from the nature of the entities:\n- **Corporate Income Tax Return**: Due on the 15th day of the fourth month after the end of the fiscal year (e.g., if the fiscal year ends on December 31, the return is due by April 15).\n- **Individual Income Tax Return**: Due on April 15 of the following year, regardless of the individual's accounting period.\n\nThis distinction is crucial for compliance and planning purposes, as corporations may have different fiscal year ends compared to individuals who typically follow the calendar year.\n\n### Practical Note\nTaxpayers should ensure they are aware of their specific filing deadlines to avoid penalties. Corporations should also consider their fiscal year-end when planning for tax payments and filings, while individuals should prepare their returns well in advance of the April 15 deadline to ensure timely compliance.",
